<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 2</p>
  <h1>Past continuous <em>was / were doing</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Open a past scene at one reference point: <span class="ex">At six, the team was finishing a report. Rina was checking the figures when the lights went out.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">open scene · bounded event</span>
    <span class="tag">was / were + verb-ing</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Open a scene at exactly 6:00 p.m.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Separate situations in progress from whole events.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control form, viewpoint, connectors, and spoken rhythm.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Reconstruct a fictional power-outage report.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can describe what was in progress at a past reference point, report the completed events around it, and ask for a missing scene detail.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a completed past action, past-be agreement, and the present-continuous frame.">
    <h3>Three checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the stated time and the complete verb system.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="finished">finished</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="finish">finish</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was">was</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="does">does</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The report marks the task complete last Friday: The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="finished" data-hint="Last Friday is a finished past frame, so use the past form finished." data-fix="The team finished the report last Friday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the report last Friday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The report locates several people in the office yesterday: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-hint="The plural subject they takes were for a past state." data-fix="They were in the office yesterday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in the office yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The live camera shows one person now: Rina <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="A present action in progress uses is plus checking." data-fix="Rina is checking the figures now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> checking the figures now.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice one scene and the events around it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Center power report</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">At 5:55 p.m., the staff members were finishing the monthly report. At 6:00, the lights went out. Rina was checking the figures, and Lee was saving the file. The generator started at 6:10. The team finished the report at 6:30.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which situations were open and already in progress at 6:00?</li>
      <li>Which verbs move the event sequence forward?</li>
      <li>Does <span class="ex">was checking</span> tell us whether Rina finished checking later?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated the open 6:00 scene from the bounded events that moved the report forward.">
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the camera view</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use continuous forms to open the scene at the reference point and past simple for each complete event.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Scene and event choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were finishing">were finishing</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="went out">went out</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was checking">was checking</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was saving">was saving</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="started">started</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="finished">finished</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The camera opens at 5:55 while the work is in progress: The staff members <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were finishing" data-hint="The plural subject staff members is inside an ongoing situation at 5:55." data-fix="The staff members were finishing the monthly report at 5:55." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the monthly report.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The outage log records one complete event at 6:00: The lights <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="went out" data-hint="The report treats the loss of power as one bounded event." data-fix="The lights went out at 6:00." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 6:00.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The camera shows Rina in the middle of a task at that moment: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was checking" data-hint="The task is open at the 6:00 reference point." data-fix="Rina was checking the figures." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the figures.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The same camera shows Lee inside another task: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was saving" data-hint="Lee’s file task is also in progress at the reference point." data-fix="Lee was saving the file." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the file.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The log records the generator’s complete start event at 6:10: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="started" data-hint="The start is presented as one bounded event at 6:10." data-fix="The generator started at 6:10." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 6:10.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The task log marks the report complete at 6:30: The team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="finished" data-hint="The report reached its completed endpoint at 6:30." data-fix="The team finished the report at 6:30." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the report then.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: open the past scene at a reference point</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The past continuous places the listener inside a situation that was in progress at a past reference point. At that point, the speaker does not show the situation’s beginning or endpoint. This is an <b>open viewpoint</b>. The past simple normally presents an event as a bounded whole and moves a report forward.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>speaker’s view</th><th>example</th><th>message</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>inside the situation at 6:00</td><td><span class="ex">At six, Rina was checking the figures.</span></td><td>checking was in progress then</td></tr>
      <tr><td>whole completed task</td><td><span class="ex">Rina checked every figure and signed the page.</span></td><td>the task is presented as bounded</td></tr>
      <tr><td>scene around an event</td><td><span class="ex">The staff members were working when the lights went out.</span></td><td>an open scene surrounds the event</td></tr>
      <tr><td>two open situations</td><td><span class="ex">Rina was calling while Lee was checking the panel.</span></td><td>both were in progress together</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">The past continuous does not promise that the situation finished later. It only keeps the situation open at the chosen reference point.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Duration does not choose the tense</h3>
    <p>A long event can be presented as a completed whole: <span class="ex">Maya worked at the center for ten years, and the job ended last year.</span> A brief repeated signal can be open at one moment: <span class="ex">At exactly six, the warning light was flashing.</span> Choose the viewpoint, not a “long action” or “short action” label.</p>
    <p>An event inside a scene is not always an interruption. It may simply occur during the scene: <span class="ex">The staff members were working when the generator started.</span></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the form: was or were plus verb-ing</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>purpose</th><th>I / he / she / it</th><th>you / we / they</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>positive</td><td><span class="ex">Rina was checking.</span></td><td><span class="ex">They were working.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative</td><td><span class="ex">She wasn’t waiting.</span></td><td><span class="ex">They weren’t waiting.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>question</td><td><span class="ex">Was Rina checking?</span></td><td><span class="ex">Were they working?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>short answer</td><td><span class="ex">Yes, she was.</span></td><td><span class="ex">No, they weren’t.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Was</span> or <span class="ex">were</span> carries subject agreement, moves before the subject in a question, and combines with <span class="ex">not</span>. Do not add <span class="ex">did</span>: say <span class="ex">Were they working?</span>, not <span class="ex">Did they were working?</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Retrieve verb-ing spelling precisely</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">work → working · make → making · sit → sitting · open → opening · lie → lying</span></p>
    <p>Drop final silent <span class="ex">e</span> in <span class="ex">making</span>. Double a final consonant after a short stressed vowel in <span class="ex">sitting</span>, but not in unstressed <span class="ex">opening</span>. Change final <span class="ex">ie</span> to <span class="ex">y</span> in <span class="ex">lying</span>. Common U.S. spelling uses one <span class="ex">l</span> in <span class="ex">traveling</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled subject agreement, polarity, question order, and two important -ing spellings.">
    <h3>Drill 1: complete the scene form</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Past-continuous form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was">was</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="weren’t">weren’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wasn’t">wasn’t</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Was">Was</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Were">Were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sitting">sitting</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lying">lying</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The camera shows several staff members at 6:00: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-hint="The plural subject they takes were in the past continuous." data-fix="They were working at 6:00." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> working.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The camera shows one warning light: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was" data-hint="The singular subject it takes was." data-fix="It was flashing." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> flashing.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The exterior camera confirms no visitors were outside: They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="weren’t" data-hint="A plural negative uses weren’t plus waiting." data-fix="They weren’t waiting outside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> waiting outside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The activity log says Rina was using the computer, not the phone: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wasn’t" data-hint="A singular negative uses wasn’t plus using." data-fix="She wasn’t using the phone." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> using the phone.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The manager asks yes or no about Rina: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Was" data-hint="A singular past-continuous question begins Was." data-fix="Was Rina checking the figures?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Rina checking the figures?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The manager asks about several staff members: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Were" data-hint="A plural past-continuous question begins Were." data-fix="Were the staff members finishing the report?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the staff members finishing the report?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>At six, Lee was seated in a chair: He was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sitting" data-hint="Sit doubles final t before -ing after its short stressed vowel." data-fix="Lee was sitting near the computer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> near the computer.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The floor camera shows one cable flat on the floor: It was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lying" data-hint="Lie changes final ie to y before -ing." data-fix="A cable was lying on the floor." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the floor.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose viewpoint before choosing a connector</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">While</span> most naturally introduces an ongoing clause: <span class="ex">While Rina was calling, Lee was checking the panel.</span> <span class="ex">When</span> can introduce a bounded event or an ongoing situation: <span class="ex">The screen went dark when the lights went out. When the team was working, the building was quiet.</span></p>
  <p><span class="ex">During</span> is followed by a noun phrase, not a complete subject-verb clause: <span class="ex">during the outage</span>, but <span class="ex">while the power was out</span>. A connector helps organize clauses; it does not select a tense automatically.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>State or activity? Meaning comes first</h3>
    <p>In neutral everyday English, basic state meanings normally stay simple: <span class="ex">Rina had a key. Lee knew the code. They needed more light.</span> Do not use <span class="ex">was having</span> for possession or <span class="ex">was knowing</span> for knowledge.</p>
    <p>The same verb can enter an activity meaning: <span class="ex">Rina was having lunch</span> means eating or experiencing the meal. <span class="ex">Lee was thinking about the problem</span> describes an active mental process. Choose from the intended meaning, not from a permanent verb blacklist.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose an open or bounded viewpoint from evidence and matched while to a clause and during to a noun.">
    <h3>Drill 2: use the stated camera or log view</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Viewpoint and connector choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was checking">was checking</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="checked">checked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="worked">worked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was flashing">was flashing</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="while">while</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="during">during</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The camera freezes at exactly 6:00 in the middle of Rina’s task: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was checking" data-hint="The task is open at the exact camera reference point." data-fix="At exactly 6:00, Rina was checking the figures." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the figures.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The checklist marks every figure complete and signed at 5:50: Rina <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="checked" data-hint="The task is presented as a completed whole before 6:00." data-fix="Rina checked every figure and signed the page at 5:50." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> every figure.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Maya’s ten-year job ended last year, so the whole period is bounded: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="worked" data-hint="A long duration can use past simple when the speaker presents the finished period as a whole." data-fix="Maya worked at the center for ten years." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> there for ten years.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The 6:00 camera shows the warning light repeatedly turning on and off: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was flashing" data-hint="The repeated signal is open and in progress at the reference point." data-fix="At 6:00, the warning light was flashing." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Both clauses describe activities in progress together: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="while" data-hint="While naturally introduces the ongoing calling clause." data-fix="While Rina was calling maintenance, Lee was checking the panel." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Rina was calling maintenance, Lee was checking the panel.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The next words form the noun phrase <b>the outage</b>: The emergency lights stayed on <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="during" data-hint="During is followed by the noun phrase the outage." data-fix="The emergency lights stayed on during the outage." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the outage.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: keep the scene light and the event clear</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In relaxed U.S. English, <span class="ex">was</span> often reduces to /wəz/ and <span class="ex">were</span> often reduces to /wɚ/ inside a statement. The activity and new event carry stronger stress: <span class="ex">Rina was <strong>CHECK</strong>ing when the lights went <strong>OUT</strong>.</span></p>
  <p>Keep <span class="ex">-ing</span> as one final nasal sound, without adding a separate hard <span class="ex">g</span>. Link a question smoothly: <span class="ex">What-were-you <strong>DO</strong>ing?</span> A short pause after an opening <span class="ex">while</span> or <span class="ex">when</span> clause helps the listener hear the scene boundary.</p>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read open-scene, bounded-event, polarity, question, state, and parallel-action listening check">
    <h2>Listen: scene, event, or state?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each fictional line once naturally and once more slowly. Listen for viewpoint, polarity, question order, and state versus activity meaning. Open the script only after checking.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard an open scene, a bounded event, polarity, question order, a state, and parallel actions.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="checking was in progress at six" data-hint="Was checking opens Rina’s task at the 6:00 reference point." data-fix="At six, Rina was checking the figures, so the task was in progress then.">
          <p class="quiz-question">1. What viewpoint does Clip 1 give?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checking was in progress at six">checking was in progress at six</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checking finished before six">checking finished before six</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checking normally happens at six">checking normally happens at six</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the task was complete at 5:50" data-hint="Checked every figure and signed the page presents the task as a bounded whole." data-fix="Rina checked every figure and signed the page at 5:50, so the task was complete then.">
          <p class="quiz-question">2. What does Clip 2 establish?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the task was complete at 5:50">the task was complete at 5:50</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the task was in progress at six">the task was in progress at six</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the task happens every day">the task happens every day</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the warning light was repeatedly on and off" data-hint="Was flashing presents the repeated signal in progress." data-fix="The warning light was flashing, so it was repeatedly turning on and off.">
          <p class="quiz-question">3. What was happening in Clip 3?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the warning light was repeatedly on and off">the warning light was repeatedly on and off</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the warning light stayed off">the warning light stayed off</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the warning light flashed once and stopped">the warning light flashed once and stopped</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the staff members were not waiting outside" data-hint="Listen for weren’t before waiting." data-fix="The staff members weren’t waiting outside.">
          <p class="quiz-question">4. What does Clip 4 report?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the staff members were not waiting outside">the staff members were not waiting outside</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the staff members were waiting outside">the staff members were waiting outside</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the visitors were not inside">the visitors were not inside</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="whether Lee was saving the file" data-hint="Was Lee saving the file requests yes or no about his ongoing task." data-fix="Was Lee saving the file? asks whether that task was in progress.">
          <p class="quiz-question">5. What information does Clip 5 request?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="whether Lee was saving the file">whether Lee was saving the file</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="why Lee saved the file">why Lee saved the file</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="when Lee finished the file">when Lee finished the file</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Rina was calling while Lee was checking" data-hint="While connects two activities that were in progress together." data-fix="Rina was calling maintenance while Lee was checking the panel.">
          <p class="quiz-question">6. Which two activities were in progress together in Clip 6?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina was calling while Lee was checking">Rina was calling while Lee was checking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rina called after Lee checked">Rina called after Lee checked</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Lee called while Rina checked">Lee called while Rina checked</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="thinking-card">
      <summary>Open the teacher script after checking</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">At six, Rina was checking the figures.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Rina checked every figure and signed the page at 5:50.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The warning light was flashing.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">The staff members weren’t waiting outside.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Was Lee saving the file?</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">While Rina was calling maintenance, Lee was checking the panel.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read a connected outage report</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>What the cameras and event log showed</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">At 5:55, the staff members were finishing a monthly report. Rina was checking the last page while Lee was saving the file. At 6:00, the lights went out and the screen went dark. The emergency lights came on immediately. While Rina was calling maintenance, Lee checked the electrical panel. The generator started at 6:10, and the team finished the report at 6:30.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You located the open scene, the first bounded event, and Lee’s activity during the call.">
    <h3>Read, then choose the exact evidence</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="finishing a monthly report" data-hint="The opening sentence states what the staff members were doing at 5:55." data-fix="At 5:55, the staff members were finishing a monthly report.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What was in progress at 5:55?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="finishing a monthly report">finishing a monthly report</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="starting the generator">starting the generator</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="leaving the building">leaving the building</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the lights went out" data-hint="The first bounded event at 6:00 is stated before the screen went dark." data-fix="At 6:00, the lights went out first.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Which bounded event does the report mention first at 6:00?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the lights went out">the lights went out</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the generator started">the generator started</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the report finished">the report finished</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="he checked the electrical panel" data-hint="The while sentence states Lee’s action during Rina’s maintenance call." data-fix="While Rina was calling maintenance, Lee checked the electrical panel.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What did Lee do while Rina was calling maintenance?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he checked the electrical panel">he checked the electrical panel</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he called maintenance">he called maintenance</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he finished the report">he finished the report</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the scene and event relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="rina was checking the figures at six" data-hint="Begin with Rina, add was checking, then the object and reference time." data-fix="Rina was checking the figures at six." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence opens Rina’s activity at the exact six o’clock reference point.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the open scene</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The 6:00 camera shows Rina in the middle of the task.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="figures">figures</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="rina">Rina</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="checking">checking</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="six">six</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="was">was</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the screen went dark while lee was saving the file" data-hint="Begin with the screen event, then add while plus Lee’s ongoing file activity." data-fix="The screen went dark while Lee was saving the file." data-success-message="Correct. The bounded screen event is related to Lee’s open file-saving situation with while.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the event inside the scene</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The screen event happened during Lee’s ongoing task.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="saving">saving</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="dark">dark</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="screen">screen</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="file">file</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="was">was</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="went">went</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="while">while</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="lee">Lee</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three high-value errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="check" data-hint="After was, the activity verb needs its -ing form." data-fix="Rina was checking the figures at six." data-why="Past continuous is was or were plus verb-ing, so check must become checking." data-success-message="Correct. You restored the required verb-ing form after was.">
    <h3>Drill 5: complete the two-part verb</h3>
    <p>The camera report says, “Rina was check the figures at six.” Tap the word to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rina">Rina</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was">was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="check">check</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="figures">the figures at six.</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="did" data-hint="A past-continuous question moves Were before the subject and does not add did." data-fix="Were the staff members working at six?" data-why="Were already carries past tense and agreement in this continuous question, so did would mix two systems." data-success-message="Correct. You removed did and used the independent were-plus-working question system.">
    <h3>Drill 6: keep one question system</h3>
    <p>The manager asks, “Did the staff members were working at six?” Tap the word to remove.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="did">Did</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="staff">the staff members</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="were">were</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="working">working at six?</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="during-clause" data-hint="During needs a noun phrase; a complete subject-verb clause uses while or when." data-fix="While the team was working, the building was quiet." data-why="The team was working is a clause, so while can introduce it. During would need a noun phrase such as during the work session." data-success-message="Correct. You matched while to the complete ongoing clause.">
    <h3>Drill 7: connector plus noun or clause?</h3>
    <p>The report says, “During the team was working, the building was quiet.” Tap the opening to repair.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="during-clause">During the team was working,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="building">the building</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was">was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="quiet">quiet.</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transform: change the viewpoint, not the facts</h3>
    <p>Say every response before revealing it.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Rina checked the figures. Open the task at 6:00.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>At 6:00, Rina was checking the figures.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Lee was saving the file. Make it negative.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Lee wasn’t saving the file.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> The staff members were working. Ask about 6:00.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Were the staff members working at 6:00?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Rina had a key. Explain why the basic possession meaning stays simple.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Had describes possession as a state here, so the neutral form is Rina had a key.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Rina was calling. Lee was checking. Connect two ongoing activities.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>While Rina was calling, Lee was checking the panel.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> The lights went out. The team was working. Put the bounded event first.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The lights went out while the team was working.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it: reconstruct a fictional incident</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real work, study, home, location, schedule, travel, family, relationships, finances, devices, health, emergencies, or difficult experiences. Use the fictional outage evidence, invent a public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Freeze the camera:</b> At 5:55 and 6:00, describe three activities already in progress. Include one negative and one question.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Move the report forward:</b> Add three bounded events from the log. Explain why duration alone does not select either tense.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Connect the evidence:</b> Use one <span class="ex">while + clause</span>, one flexible <span class="ex">when</span> clause, and one <span class="ex">during + noun phrase</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a fictional power-outage report for 45–60 seconds.</b> Establish one exact reference time; describe at least three open situations; add three bounded events in order; include a negative or question; use <span class="ex">while</span> or <span class="ex">when</span> accurately; and end with one unresolved detail for the listener to ask about.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled open viewpoint, bounded events, form, state meaning, and clause connectors.">
    <h3>Eight decisions from a new incident report</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="was checking" data-hint="The camera freezes in the middle of Maya’s task at exactly 8:00." data-fix="At exactly 8:00, Maya was checking the doors.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. The camera freezes at exactly 8:00 while Maya’s task is open: She ___ the doors.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was checking">was checking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checked">checked</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checks">checks</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="checked" data-hint="The log marks the door check complete at 8:05." data-fix="Maya checked every door and signed the log at 8:05.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The log marks the whole task complete at 8:05: Maya ___ every door and signed the page.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="checked">checked</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was checking">was checking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is checking">is checking</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="were" data-hint="The plural subject they takes were before waiting." data-fix="They were waiting near the entrance.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The camera shows two visitors at that moment: They ___ waiting near the entrance.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="were">were</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was">was</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="did">did</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Were the visitors waiting?" data-hint="A plural past-continuous question moves Were before the subject." data-fix="Were the visitors waiting?">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Which question asks whether the visitors’ wait was in progress?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Were the visitors waiting?">Were the visitors waiting?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Did the visitors were waiting?">Did the visitors were waiting?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Were the visitors wait?">Were the visitors wait?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="wasn’t listening" data-hint="One person in a negative ongoing situation takes wasn’t plus listening." data-fix="Lee wasn’t listening when the announcement began.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. The report says Lee missed the announcement because the activity was not in progress: He ___ when it began.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="wasn’t listening">wasn’t listening</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="didn’t listening">didn’t listening</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="weren’t listening">weren’t listening</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="knew" data-hint="Basic knowledge is a state here, so neutral everyday English uses past simple knew." data-fix="Rina knew the access code.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. The report describes possession of information, not an active thinking process: Rina ___ the access code.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="knew">knew</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was knowing">was knowing</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="was know">was know</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="during" data-hint="The outage is a noun phrase, so during can introduce it." data-fix="The emergency lights stayed on during the outage.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. The next words form the noun phrase <b>the outage</b>: The emergency lights stayed on ___ the outage.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="during">during</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="while">while</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="when">when</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="when" data-hint="The alarm rang once as a bounded event, so when naturally introduces it in this report." data-fix="Maya was checking the doors when the alarm rang once at 8:02.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. The log records one alarm ring at 8:02: Maya was checking the doors ___ the alarm rang once.</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="when">when</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="during">during</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="because">because</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
